WEBVTT

00:00:01.340 --> 00:00:05.360
<i>Karibuchi Takami was dispatched from Fusou</i>

00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:02.730
<b>Best Wishes in Battle</b>

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:09.320
<i>to the 502nd Joint Fighter Wing, 
the Brave Witches.</i>

00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:13.800
<i>But during a Neuroi attack on 
the fleet, she was wounded.</i>

00:00:14.230 --> 00:00:18.780
<i>Her sister, Hikari, volunteered to 
go in her place.</i>

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:22.080
If you want to fight, 
you have to get stronger.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:58.010
<b>Episode 3
"The 502nd Joint Fighter Wing"</b>

00:01:58.180 --> 00:02:02.140
<b>Orussia Empire   Petersburg
502nd Joint Fighter Wing Base</b>

00:01:58.470 --> 00:02:02.720
Sub-lieutenant Karibuchi Takami's 
younger sister from Fusou

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:05.210
is joining us in her stead.

00:02:05.210 --> 00:02:06.660
I'm Karibuchi Hikari.

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:09.770
I'll do my best in my sister's place.

00:02:11.510 --> 00:02:14.340
I'm Gundula Rall, the commander of the 502nd.

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:15.980
My rank is flight leader.

00:02:16.310 --> 00:02:22.100
I am Flight Lieutenant Aleksandra 
Ivanovna Pokryshkin.

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:25.090
Flying Officer Waltrud Krupinski.

00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:27.270
Will you call me "Countess"?

00:02:27.270 --> 00:02:30.030
Countess? Are you really important?

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:32.930
Feel free to ignore her jokes.

00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:35.280
That's terrible, Sensei.

00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:36.770
Sensei?

00:02:36.770 --> 00:02:39.650
I'm Flight Sergeant Edytha Rossmann.

00:02:39.650 --> 00:02:42.170
I'm the wing's instructor.

00:02:42.820 --> 00:02:46.000
Georgette Lemare. I'm a pilot officer.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:48.310
Shimohara Sadako. I'm a pilot officer.

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:51.740
Hey, it's your turn, Kanno.

00:02:51.740 --> 00:02:52.600
I don't care.

00:02:55.580 --> 00:02:59.230
Um, next to me is Pilot Officer Kanno Naoe.

00:02:59.230 --> 00:03:02.380
I'm Flight Sergeant Nikka Edvardine Katajainen.

00:03:02.380 --> 00:03:03.730
Call me "Nipa."

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:05.970
Okay, introductions are finished.

00:03:05.970 --> 00:03:07.480
Let's eat.

00:03:08.740 --> 00:03:09.990
Hey, Karibuchi-san.

00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:12.430
Can I call you Hikari-chan?

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:13.370
Huh?

00:03:16.310 --> 00:03:17.750
She's asleep...

00:03:18.020 --> 00:03:20.780
The little kitty must be really tired.

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:24.650
What's so funny?

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:26.840
A core?

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:33.300
I'm sure I saw a core...

00:03:33.550 --> 00:03:35.850
What was that?

00:03:38.830 --> 00:03:40.730
Good morning, Sis.

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:42.870
I'll do my best, okay?

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:46.450
Okay!

00:03:53.210 --> 00:03:55.090
It's gotten pretty cold.

00:03:55.090 --> 00:03:56.540
Has it?

00:03:57.160 --> 00:03:59.500
I shouldn't have asked a Suomusian.

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:00.120
Huh?

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:01.950
Someone's running up ahead.

00:04:03.070 --> 00:04:04.640
It's Karibuchi-san.

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:05.750
Let's pass her.

00:04:10.010 --> 00:04:11.270
Good morning!

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:12.180
Morning!

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:13.240
Training?

00:04:13.240 --> 00:04:13.760
Yes.

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:15.050
You're slow, Nipa!

00:04:15.270 --> 00:04:17.050
What's your problem? Jeez.

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:23.730
Karibuchi-san's following us.

00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:27.610
A beginner can't keep up with our pace.

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:31.870
Karibuchi?

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:32.610
Yes.

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:36.290
I can't go on...

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:38.050
Damn it!

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:42.660
Hey! You!

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:46.420
I refuse to accept it!

00:04:46.420 --> 00:04:49.090
You can't take Takami's place!

00:04:50.450 --> 00:04:53.680
She and I were going to 
destroy the Neuroi nest!

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:56.230
But because you were weak...

00:04:56.540 --> 00:04:57.670
You're right.

00:04:57.910 --> 00:04:59.140
It's my fault.

00:04:59.430 --> 00:05:01.600
It happened to my sister because I was weak.

00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:04.690
But I'll work hard and get stronger!

00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:07.950
If working hard were all it took 
to get stronger, it'd be easy!

00:05:08.230 --> 00:05:10.230
Right now, we need someone ready to fight.

00:05:10.230 --> 00:05:11.780
We won't know until we try!

00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:14.540
Hey, you two.

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:16.160
No fighting.

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:17.250
We're all comrades.

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:18.200
We are not!

00:05:18.820 --> 00:05:21.650
The weak put others in danger, too.

00:05:21.790 --> 00:05:24.680
If you want to befriend someone, 
go back to Fusou already!

00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:26.130
Kanno!

00:05:27.190 --> 00:05:28.690
I-I'm sorry.

00:05:28.690 --> 00:05:32.150
She can be really mean, but she 
isn't a bad person.

00:05:32.150 --> 00:05:35.640
It's like... In her own way, 
she's struggling hard.

00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:36.920
I know.

00:05:37.130 --> 00:05:39.350
If only I were stronger...

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:45.320
By the way, Karibuchi-san, are you 
a marathon runner or something?

00:05:45.460 --> 00:05:46.640
No.

00:05:46.640 --> 00:05:50.180
I just used to run to bring my dad his lunch.

00:05:50.670 --> 00:05:51.750
Lunch?

00:05:51.880 --> 00:05:52.900
Yes.

00:05:54.090 --> 00:05:55.380
That's funny.

00:05:57.730 --> 00:06:00.020
You fell asleep while eating yesterday, right?

00:06:00.020 --> 00:06:01.990
It's almost breakfast time. Let's go back.

00:06:01.990 --> 00:06:03.770
Um, Nipa-san...

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:08.020
Thank you for saying that we're comrades.

00:06:09.210 --> 00:06:10.260
Let's go.

00:06:12.130 --> 00:06:14.240
It seems she has a lot of basic stamina.

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:22.390
You eat a lot.

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:25.080
I need to eat a lot and get strong.

00:06:25.080 --> 00:06:26.830
Is the taste to your liking?

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:28.580
It's delicious.

00:06:28.580 --> 00:06:30.450
Did you make it, Shimohara-san?

00:06:30.630 --> 00:06:31.390
Yes.

00:06:31.390 --> 00:06:33.120
There's a cooking crew,

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:35.280
but I like to cook.

00:06:35.280 --> 00:06:38.950
These penny buns go well with 
the butter, don't they?

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:43.490
Nipa-san picked them in Shuvalov Park.  

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:47.140
Maybe we'll have chanterelles 
or truffles next time.

00:06:47.360 --> 00:06:48.500
Truffles...

00:06:48.500 --> 00:06:52.930
But if you break another Unit, I'll forbid 
you from mushroom hunting.

00:06:53.420 --> 00:06:54.880
That isn't fair!

00:06:55.150 --> 00:06:57.460
Um, are there seconds?

00:06:57.460 --> 00:06:59.630
Yes, there's plenty.

00:07:00.440 --> 00:07:03.350
Girls who eat a lot are cute.

00:07:04.120 --> 00:07:05.790
Cute?

00:07:07.370 --> 00:07:12.680
Right now, we're looking at our 
former primary targets,

00:07:12.890 --> 00:07:14.780
Neuroi nests Anna and Vzsily.

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:18.450
There's also the new nest in the White Sea...

00:07:18.610 --> 00:07:20.450
Another bad spot....

00:07:20.540 --> 00:07:24.990
Very well, we will name 
the new nest "Grigori."

00:07:24.990 --> 00:07:29.140
The area affected by Neuroi emerging 
from Grigori is expanding rapidly.

00:07:29.140 --> 00:07:31.960
It threatens to cut off our supply lines.

00:07:32.810 --> 00:07:36.630
If our supply lines are cut, we will be 
forced to withdraw from this base.

00:07:36.890 --> 00:07:38.880
Well, that sucks.

00:07:38.880 --> 00:07:40.970
This is pretty dire news, huh?

00:07:40.970 --> 00:07:46.810
That means we need to neutralize 
Grigori at once.

00:07:47.030 --> 00:07:48.040
Um...

00:07:48.390 --> 00:07:50.840
Is it possible to defeat a Neuroi nest?

00:07:51.220 --> 00:07:55.390
You were told that the 501st 
wiped out the Gallia nest.

00:07:55.650 --> 00:07:58.000
But how?

00:07:58.000 --> 00:08:00.150
Supposedly, it's top secret.

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:01.610
Damn it.

00:08:01.950 --> 00:08:05.760
But if the 501st can do it, so can we.

00:08:06.350 --> 00:08:07.660
I'll crush it.

00:08:08.510 --> 00:08:09.830
That's the spirit, Kanno.

00:08:10.070 --> 00:08:10.870
Karibuchi...

00:08:10.870 --> 00:08:12.200
Y-Yes!

00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:13.990
You start training this afternoon.

00:08:14.230 --> 00:08:16.650
Until then, have someone show 
you around the base.

00:08:16.650 --> 00:08:17.340
Yes, ma'am!

00:08:17.910 --> 00:08:19.130
Ah...

00:08:19.250 --> 00:08:21.760
Georgette-san, can you do it?

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:26.390
U-Um, I have something to do.

00:08:26.390 --> 00:08:27.280
I see.

00:08:27.280 --> 00:08:28.940
Nipa-san, then.

00:08:29.100 --> 00:08:29.960
Sure.

00:08:30.820 --> 00:08:31.760
All right.

00:08:31.760 --> 00:08:34.230
Everyone, follow the duty schedule.

00:08:55.530 --> 00:08:57.200
What a view!

00:08:57.200 --> 00:09:00.090
This is the area's tallest building.

00:09:00.090 --> 00:09:02.510
What a big town!

00:09:02.510 --> 00:09:06.800
Before the Neuroi came, two million 
people lived in Petersburg.

00:09:06.800 --> 00:09:08.440
That many?

00:09:08.440 --> 00:09:13.460
But everyone has evacuated now, except the 
soldiers needed to maintain this base.

00:09:13.660 --> 00:09:16.540
This is a front-line base against the Neuroi.

00:09:16.890 --> 00:09:19.100
A huge town like this...

00:09:19.100 --> 00:09:20.220
It's Kanno.

00:09:23.750 --> 00:09:24.870
Kanno-san...

00:09:24.870 --> 00:09:28.380
She must have been really upset 
that Karibuchi-san outran her...

00:09:29.600 --> 00:09:30.730
Never mind.

00:09:30.730 --> 00:09:32.760
You shouldn't try to copy her.

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:36.690
Rossmann-sensei has instructed 
us all to avoid overwork.

00:09:40.100 --> 00:09:45.100
<b>The 501st Joint Fighter Wing
Strike Witches

00:09:50.110 --> 00:09:51.860
<b>Chidori</b>

00:09:52.010 --> 00:09:54.650
Chidori, I'm about to start training.

00:09:54.650 --> 00:09:56.270
Let's do our best together!

00:09:56.860 --> 00:09:58.600
I'll do my best, too!

00:09:56.860 --> 00:10:00.240
<b>Chidori</b>

00:09:58.600 --> 00:10:00.230
Is that how she'd talk?

00:10:00.230 --> 00:10:01.730
What are you doing?

00:10:01.730 --> 00:10:05.400
U-Um, my sister told me to 
listen to my Unit's voice.

00:10:05.640 --> 00:10:07.700
You seem to have a lot of endurance.

00:10:09.880 --> 00:10:12.530
You have completed basic 
and intermediate training.

00:10:12.530 --> 00:10:14.000
Your grades are F-rank.

00:10:14.320 --> 00:10:16.530
This document is useless.

00:10:16.970 --> 00:10:18.380
Put on your Unit.

00:10:18.510 --> 00:10:19.350
Yes!

00:10:24.660 --> 00:10:25.750
Start engine.

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:29.910
Magical power mixture at 9:1.

00:10:29.910 --> 00:10:31.840
Keep RPMs at 1,500.

00:10:32.100 --> 00:10:32.770
Right!

00:10:34.500 --> 00:10:37.770
Your base and peak RPMs are 1,000 apart.

00:10:37.770 --> 00:10:39.500
Focus more on training.

00:10:39.500 --> 00:10:40.660
This is terrible.

00:10:40.660 --> 00:10:41.780
Increase them to 2,000.

00:10:41.780 --> 00:10:42.530
Yes!

00:10:44.820 --> 00:10:46.280
This is Fusou's latest model.

00:10:46.280 --> 00:10:48.800
2,000 hp and a top speed of 600 km/h.

00:10:49.100 --> 00:10:51.170
Its operational distance is in 
the 2,000-kilometer class.

00:10:51.310 --> 00:10:53.780
I can't wait to see how it flies.

00:10:53.780 --> 00:10:54.540
Take off!

00:11:03.710 --> 00:11:05.650
I thought she increased them to 2,000.

00:11:05.940 --> 00:11:07.760
She isn't accelerating well.

00:11:08.140 --> 00:11:12.230
Go to an altitude of 300, and do a 
lap around the base's exterior.

00:11:12.230 --> 00:11:14.500
Then pass over the runway 
airspace at top speed.

00:11:14.670 --> 00:11:15.350
Yes!

00:11:20.860 --> 00:11:23.520
Is Fusou's new Unit defective?

00:11:23.520 --> 00:11:25.530
It isn't the machine's fault.

00:11:25.530 --> 00:11:27.770
She simply lacks the requisite magical power.

00:11:28.240 --> 00:11:29.110
That's fine.

00:11:29.110 --> 00:11:30.130
Come back.

00:11:30.740 --> 00:11:31.820
Already?

00:11:31.820 --> 00:11:32.650
That's right.

00:11:32.650 --> 00:11:33.710
I've seen enough.

00:11:35.130 --> 00:11:36.020
Yes.

00:11:37.220 --> 00:11:39.110
Try spinning it at full power.

00:11:39.110 --> 00:11:39.940
Yes!

00:11:43.940 --> 00:11:44.870
I knew it.

00:11:44.870 --> 00:11:47.910
You don't reach the magical 
power this Unit requires.

00:11:48.090 --> 00:11:49.800
That's strange...

00:11:49.800 --> 00:11:51.260
I was able to fly with it.

00:11:51.480 --> 00:11:52.710
You weren't.

00:11:52.710 --> 00:11:54.230
It was letting you fly.

00:11:55.130 --> 00:11:57.610
This is Takami's new Unit, right?

00:11:57.610 --> 00:11:59.030
An amateur can't control it.

00:11:59.030 --> 00:11:59.990
I'll use it.

00:11:59.990 --> 00:12:00.570
No!

00:12:00.800 --> 00:12:02.770
Chidori belongs to my sister and me.

00:12:02.770 --> 00:12:03.980
What the hell is Chidori?

00:12:03.980 --> 00:12:04.610
Shut up!

00:12:04.860 --> 00:12:09.980
We'll issue orders later regarding 
assignment for the new Unit.

00:12:09.980 --> 00:12:11.650
I'm sure she can't use it.

00:12:11.650 --> 00:12:13.270
We don't know that!

00:12:13.270 --> 00:12:14.350
What are you talking about?

00:12:14.350 --> 00:12:16.040
You can't even spin the engine!

00:12:16.040 --> 00:12:17.190
That's...

00:12:18.690 --> 00:12:21.100
I have to get stronger.

00:12:21.200 --> 00:12:24.170
Takami isn't here, and there's a new nest.

00:12:24.440 --> 00:12:28.500
In this situation, an amateur like 
her will just be a handicap!

00:12:28.620 --> 00:12:31.150
Squadron Leader Rall will make that decision.

00:12:32.050 --> 00:12:32.980
Damn it!

00:12:33.470 --> 00:12:34.980
So, how did it go?

00:12:35.270 --> 00:12:37.130
Right now, she isn't ready for combat.

00:12:37.310 --> 00:12:39.810
It would be best to send 
her back immediately.

00:12:40.430 --> 00:12:42.010
I agree.

00:12:42.140 --> 00:12:45.160
This base doesn't have room for a novice.

00:12:46.050 --> 00:12:47.360
It's unfortunate.

00:12:47.460 --> 00:12:50.270
They were probably after the Fusou supplies.

00:12:50.270 --> 00:12:50.730
Um!

00:12:50.900 --> 00:12:54.240
I saw a Neuroi core in the last fight!

00:12:54.240 --> 00:12:55.320
What?

00:12:55.320 --> 00:12:56.640
If that's true,

00:12:56.640 --> 00:12:59.880
it explains how you survived 
the Neuroi for five minutes.

00:13:00.010 --> 00:13:03.910
If she's the sister of Sub-lieutenant Karibuchi, 
the one with magic eyes, it's possible.

00:13:03.910 --> 00:13:04.960
Interesting.

00:13:05.370 --> 00:13:07.590
Sensei, take a look.

00:13:07.590 --> 00:13:08.530
Roger.

00:13:10.310 --> 00:13:11.790
Emergency sortie!

00:13:12.310 --> 00:13:13.810
<b>Chidori</b>

00:13:16.650 --> 00:13:18.020
The enemy is a single medium-size.

00:13:18.020 --> 00:13:21.250
It's heading toward us from Grigori, 
at an altitude of 3,000 meters.

00:13:21.250 --> 00:13:23.480
Its speed is 300 km/h.

00:13:23.480 --> 00:13:24.850
Fifteen minutes until arrival.

00:13:25.460 --> 00:13:27.790
Flying Officer Krupinski will be my wingman.

00:13:27.790 --> 00:13:29.670
Kanno and Nipa will take the front.

00:13:29.670 --> 00:13:31.490
Shimohara and Georgette will stand by here.

00:13:31.730 --> 00:13:34.000
Hikari-san, you launch, too.

00:13:35.200 --> 00:13:36.010
Yes, ma'am!

00:13:36.150 --> 00:13:37.650
Why her?

00:13:37.650 --> 00:13:39.200
It's part of her training.

00:13:39.200 --> 00:13:40.470
I authorize it.

00:13:41.420 --> 00:13:42.340
Roger...

00:13:42.790 --> 00:13:47.220
Obey my orders, and do not leave the 
second position for any reason.

00:13:47.220 --> 00:13:48.210
Yes, ma'am!

00:13:55.780 --> 00:13:56.820
Enemy sighted!

00:13:56.820 --> 00:13:58.100
All Witches, charge!

00:13:58.100 --> 00:13:59.260
Roger!

00:14:03.570 --> 00:14:05.400
Hikari-san, can you see the core?

00:14:07.400 --> 00:14:08.720
Well? Can you?

00:14:08.720 --> 00:14:09.490
Can't you?

00:14:11.260 --> 00:14:12.350
I can't...

00:14:13.670 --> 00:14:14.540
I see.

00:14:14.720 --> 00:14:15.780
That's enough.

00:14:15.910 --> 00:14:17.050
Fall back.

00:14:17.580 --> 00:14:18.450
Yes.

00:14:20.350 --> 00:14:21.410
Watch out!

00:14:24.430 --> 00:14:25.460
Karibuchi-san!

00:14:27.580 --> 00:14:28.830
Run, fool!

00:14:35.310 --> 00:14:36.190
Kanno-san!

00:14:36.190 --> 00:14:37.640
Are you trying to get killed?

00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:39.760
You should have listened!

00:14:39.760 --> 00:14:40.470
Nipa!

00:14:40.470 --> 00:14:41.100
Roger!

00:14:50.730 --> 00:14:51.520
Take this!

00:15:04.520 --> 00:15:05.540
Kanno-san!

00:15:06.040 --> 00:15:08.000
Thank you for saving me.

00:15:08.100 --> 00:15:09.870
I didn't save you.

00:15:09.870 --> 00:15:12.180
I just don't want the new Unit destroyed.

00:15:12.180 --> 00:15:14.230
Kanno-san and Nipa-san,

00:15:14.230 --> 00:15:16.560
search the area for more enemies.

00:15:16.560 --> 00:15:18.010
Everyone else, head back.

00:15:18.360 --> 00:15:19.620
Roger.

00:15:20.340 --> 00:15:23.370
It seems what you saw wasn't a core, was it?

00:15:33.280 --> 00:15:35.580
<b>Chidori</b>

00:15:34.100 --> 00:15:35.570
Hey, Chidori...

00:15:35.780 --> 00:15:38.590
I know what I saw was a core.

00:15:38.710 --> 00:15:40.570
But why was I able to see it?

00:15:40.750 --> 00:15:41.800
Well?

00:15:41.800 --> 00:15:42.970
Unfortunately...

00:15:43.330 --> 00:15:44.240
I see.

00:15:45.610 --> 00:15:47.000
Sergeant Karibuchi Hikari.

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:48.090
Yes, ma'am!

00:15:48.090 --> 00:15:51.100
Commander Rall, Flight Sergeant 
Nikka collapsed again.

00:15:51.270 --> 00:15:54.320
The cause was a locust swarm getting 
into her coolant unit again.

00:15:54.320 --> 00:15:55.680
What?

00:15:55.680 --> 00:15:57.850
She has the worst luck.

00:15:57.850 --> 00:15:59.110
Where's the recovery team?

00:15:59.110 --> 00:16:01.090
They say it's hard to pinpoint her crash point.

00:16:01.510 --> 00:16:04.100
And it will take time to locate 
her from the ground.

00:16:04.440 --> 00:16:06.860
She probably won't make it in time for dinner.

00:16:06.980 --> 00:16:08.710
I'll go help her.

00:16:08.710 --> 00:16:09.940
Even if you go...

00:16:09.940 --> 00:16:10.800
Very well.

00:16:10.800 --> 00:16:11.780
I permit it.

00:16:11.780 --> 00:16:13.110
Thank you!

00:16:13.110 --> 00:16:16.620
Pilot Officer Kanno is currently 
above Lake Ladoga.

00:16:16.750 --> 00:16:17.950
Go with her.

00:16:18.190 --> 00:16:18.990
Yes, ma'am!

00:16:22.450 --> 00:16:23.950
Was that a good idea?

00:16:24.310 --> 00:16:27.240
There's no harm in letting her 
take home some memories.

00:16:27.610 --> 00:16:29.880
Get the paperwork ready to 
send her back to Fusou.

00:16:30.400 --> 00:16:31.160
Yes, ma'am.

00:16:31.340 --> 00:16:33.630
<b>Lake Ladoga</b>

00:16:33.840 --> 00:16:35.300
You again?

00:16:35.300 --> 00:16:36.340
What are you doing here?

00:16:36.340 --> 00:16:38.220
I'll look for Nipa-san, too.

00:16:38.220 --> 00:16:39.360
You'll slow me down.

00:16:39.360 --> 00:16:40.810
I'm better off on my own.

00:16:41.780 --> 00:16:43.390
No fighting.

00:16:43.390 --> 00:16:44.550
We're all comrades.

00:16:45.010 --> 00:16:46.090
We're comrades.

00:16:46.090 --> 00:16:47.060
I have to help her.

00:16:52.250 --> 00:16:54.220
She should be around here.

00:16:54.450 --> 00:16:57.320
She should build a fire
or something, at least.

00:16:57.530 --> 00:16:58.840
Nipa-san!

00:16:58.840 --> 00:17:00.450
Where are you?

00:17:02.700 --> 00:17:05.390
Oh, no... My eyes are getting blurry.

00:17:05.790 --> 00:17:07.740
Nipa-san!

00:17:07.740 --> 00:17:10.670
She has lots of stamina, even if 
that's all she has.

00:17:10.770 --> 00:17:12.670
Nipa-san!

00:17:14.620 --> 00:17:15.840
I found her!

00:17:15.840 --> 00:17:16.840
You did?

00:17:19.750 --> 00:17:20.630
Nipa!

00:17:20.630 --> 00:17:22.280
Nipa-san!

00:17:22.280 --> 00:17:23.920
Hey, Nipa, are you okay?

00:17:26.820 --> 00:17:27.800
She's fine.

00:17:27.800 --> 00:17:28.690
She's alive.

00:17:29.630 --> 00:17:32.060
Good... You worried me.

00:17:32.870 --> 00:17:34.530
Wh-What?

00:17:34.840 --> 00:17:36.690
Nothing.

00:17:38.930 --> 00:17:40.830
Oh... Kanno.

00:17:40.830 --> 00:17:42.500
What do you mean by, "Oh... Kanno"?

00:17:42.500 --> 00:17:43.760
I was worried about you.

00:17:43.760 --> 00:17:45.460
I'm glad you're safe!

00:17:45.460 --> 00:17:48.020
You were late, so I fell asleep.

00:17:49.760 --> 00:17:51.590
I broke another one.

00:17:51.790 --> 00:17:54.290
There's kneeling waiting for me at home, huh?

00:17:54.290 --> 00:17:55.370
Kneeling?

00:17:55.370 --> 00:17:56.480
Just come on.

00:17:56.480 --> 00:17:58.670
Let's return before it gets late.

00:17:59.620 --> 00:18:01.330
I'm hungry.

00:18:01.330 --> 00:18:02.360
Let's hurry.

00:18:02.360 --> 00:18:03.180
Right!

00:18:04.680 --> 00:18:05.700
Kanno, below us!

00:18:05.700 --> 00:18:06.310
What?

00:18:08.600 --> 00:18:09.630
Neuroi!

00:18:09.630 --> 00:18:10.530
Damn it!

00:18:10.530 --> 00:18:11.920
Where did they come from?

00:18:11.920 --> 00:18:13.200
The nest is nearby.

00:18:13.200 --> 00:18:14.240
It might be a new attack wave.

00:18:14.390 --> 00:18:16.410
I'm the only one who can fight, huh?

00:18:16.410 --> 00:18:17.900
You take care of Nipa!

00:18:18.100 --> 00:18:19.320
Hey, Kanno!

00:18:19.320 --> 00:18:20.890
You go home!

00:18:21.560 --> 00:18:22.900
Kanno-san!

00:18:25.530 --> 00:18:26.890
She's so high....

00:18:26.890 --> 00:18:28.340
At least ten thousand meters.

00:18:28.340 --> 00:18:29.620
There isn't enough air up there!

00:18:33.460 --> 00:18:34.250
Damn it!

00:18:34.250 --> 00:18:35.490
The engine!

00:18:40.670 --> 00:18:41.510
Damn it!

00:18:41.510 --> 00:18:44.080
At this height, the Unit won't listen to me!

00:18:44.080 --> 00:18:45.550
I can't breathe, either!

00:18:49.590 --> 00:18:50.710
This is bad.

00:18:51.140 --> 00:18:54.420
The Neuroi is stopping Kanno 
from coming back down!

00:18:54.760 --> 00:18:57.390
Damn it all! Work! Work!

00:18:57.390 --> 00:18:58.410
Nipa-san...

00:18:59.800 --> 00:19:01.550
Where are you going, Karibuchi-san?

00:19:01.550 --> 00:19:03.620
I'm going to save her!

00:19:03.620 --> 00:19:05.620
Carrying me, you won't be able to!

00:19:05.620 --> 00:19:06.990
But I'm going, anyway!

00:19:18.150 --> 00:19:19.780
Let's get rid of my Unit.

00:19:19.780 --> 00:19:21.490
That'll make it a lot lighter!

00:19:21.490 --> 00:19:22.400
No!

00:19:22.400 --> 00:19:24.080
I won't let you!

00:19:28.930 --> 00:19:31.680
If I can just distract it for one second...

00:19:34.180 --> 00:19:35.720
Kanno!

00:19:35.990 --> 00:19:36.970
You guys!

00:19:45.270 --> 00:19:46.200
Now!

00:19:50.040 --> 00:19:51.930
<i>Tsurugi Issen!</i>

00:19:57.470 --> 00:19:58.660
You did it!

00:20:07.830 --> 00:20:10.030
I see one pair of wing lights!

00:20:10.030 --> 00:20:10.850
One?

00:20:15.470 --> 00:20:16.490
I can see them!

00:20:16.490 --> 00:20:17.500
All three are there!

00:20:17.500 --> 00:20:18.670
Good.

00:20:18.670 --> 00:20:19.990
Everyone's safe.

00:20:19.990 --> 00:20:21.870
Yes! We're here!

00:20:22.160 --> 00:20:23.670
Good grief...

00:20:23.670 --> 00:20:25.610
I'm hungry, aren't you?

00:20:33.600 --> 00:20:34.560
They fell.

00:20:35.710 --> 00:20:37.960
All three of you, kneel!

00:20:41.390 --> 00:20:42.710
What are you looking at?

00:20:42.710 --> 00:20:45.460
It's so amazing that you punched a Neuroi!

00:20:45.460 --> 00:20:46.530
You can't have it.

00:20:46.530 --> 00:20:48.090
I didn't ask that.

00:20:48.470 --> 00:20:51.440
I've used this to defeat all kinds of Neuroi.

00:20:51.830 --> 00:20:54.430
I won't give it to anyone.

00:20:54.620 --> 00:20:58.100
Anyway, Kanno, don't you have 
something to say to Hikari?

00:20:58.100 --> 00:21:01.490
Well, it appears you have stamina and guts.

00:21:01.490 --> 00:21:02.860
Really?

00:21:02.860 --> 00:21:03.790
Is that all?

00:21:03.790 --> 00:21:04.810
Shut up!

00:21:04.810 --> 00:21:06.100
That's all she has!

00:21:06.100 --> 00:21:08.060
I refuse to accept her.

00:21:08.270 --> 00:21:11.500
After she saved you, you don't 
need to say that!

00:21:11.500 --> 00:21:12.140
What?!

00:21:12.190 --> 00:21:13.210
What?

00:21:13.210 --> 00:21:15.220
No fighting!

00:21:15.220 --> 00:21:18.060
Pilot Officer Kanno to the command room!

00:21:19.230 --> 00:21:21.550
You three worked together to shoot it down?

00:21:21.830 --> 00:21:23.560
Maybe.

00:21:23.560 --> 00:21:26.060
But I'm sure I would have won without her!

00:21:26.380 --> 00:21:27.750
I see.

00:21:28.160 --> 00:21:31.140
In the end, she was useful.

00:21:31.330 --> 00:21:32.300
Yeah...

00:21:32.300 --> 00:21:34.840
But I would have beaten it without her.

00:21:35.590 --> 00:21:38.050
Sensei, you can have her for a week.

00:21:38.050 --> 00:21:38.750
Yes, ma'am.

00:21:52.030 --> 00:21:55.040
<b>To Be Continued</b>

00:23:26.210 --> 00:23:27.710
On a tough battlefield,

00:23:27.710 --> 00:23:29.400
if you lack the power to fight,

00:23:29.400 --> 00:23:31.870
you and those around you will be sad.

00:23:32.150 --> 00:23:34.750
I don't want anyone else to 
experience that sadness.

00:23:35.380 --> 00:23:39.100
Next time on <i>Brave Witches</i>: 
If You Want to Fight, Get Stronger!

00:23:37.850 --> 00:23:40.050
<b>Episode 4
"If You Want to Fight, Get Stronger!"</b>
